1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,119
Question ten.

2
00:00:01,119 --> 00:00:07,492
Step one: macro scan. It asks which check tests that fields are not blank.

3
00:00:07,492 --> 00:00:10,506
One mark. Command words: “this is”.

4
00:00:10,506 --> 00:00:12,056
Step two: denoise.

5
00:00:12,056 --> 00:00:14,983
Useful, in yellow: certain fields.

6
00:00:14,983 --> 00:00:18,772
In cyan: “required” and “must not be blank”.

7
00:00:18,772 --> 00:00:23,939
Useless red herring: the inter-school contest — kick it out.

8
00:00:23,939 --> 00:00:25,489
Step three: draft.

9
00:00:25,489 --> 00:00:27,814
Only checks: filled or not?

10
00:00:27,814 --> 00:00:30,311
Filled or not means presence.

11
00:00:30,311 --> 00:00:31,603
Presence check.

12
00:00:31,603 --> 00:00:33,067
Step four: P O E.

13
00:00:33,067 --> 00:00:36,855
B, range check: no bounds in the stem — cut.

14
00:00:36,855 --> 00:00:40,214
C, type check: not checking type — cut.

15
00:00:40,214 --> 00:00:44,347
D, check digit: no check code in the stem — cut.

16
00:00:44,347 --> 00:00:52,011
Step five: sanity check and lock. “Must not be blank” matches the presence check exactly.

17
00:00:52,011 --> 00:00:54,336
So the correct answer is A.

